'''CH-33Z''' was a [[MSE-6 series repair droid|MSE-6 series]] [[Maintenance droid|repair]] [[droid]]. At one point, the [[Chadra-Fan]] [[Vosa (Chadra-Fan)|Vosa]] stood atop the [[MSE series]] droid at the [[Day Star Hotel]] while she spoke to her [[spy]], [[Faddey]].<ref name="JTC-E4" /> In the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]], CH-33Z was scurrying around the halls of the [[New Republic Correctional Transport]] ''[[Bothan-5]]'' when he was shot and destroyed by [[Burg]], a member of [[Ranzar Malk]]'s [[Ranzar Malk's crew|crew]] of [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] who were there to [[Bothan-Five incident|rescue]] the prisoner [[Qin]]. CH-33Z's destruction alerted [[N5 sentry droid]]s to the crew's presence.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

==Behind the scenes==
===Origin===
[[File:CH-33Z_The_Star_Wars_Show.jpg|thumb|left|200px|CH-33Z with his appearance from ''The Mandalorian'' in ''The Star Wars Show''.]]
CH-33Z "Cheeze" originated as a recurring side character on the online variety news show ''[[The Star Wars Show]]'', interacting with the show's hosts as its resident sound expert and "mouse droid extraordinaire." He made his first appearance in the show's debut episode on [[May 11]], [[2016]], though unnamed at the time, as his name was left up to fans to decide through social media.<ref name="Star Wars Show Ep1">{{StarWarsShow|dcj_IRwHYPI|Duncan Jones, The Best of Star Wars Day, and Celebration Europe News|sw_url=video/the-star-wars-show-episode-1}}</ref> After receiving many humorous suggestions such as "Mon Mousema," "Mouse Eisley," "Mouse Windu," and "Mouse Kanata," hosts [[Peter Townley]] and [[Andi Gutierrez]] announced at the end of the show's second episode on [[May 18]], 2016 that the mouse droid had officially been named "CH-33Z" or "Cheeze," based on the suggestion<ref name="CH-33Z Origin">{{Twitter|storydroid|status/730508972743135232|COLIN BISHOP|quote=@starwars #StarWarsShow that mouse droid should be CH-33Z (cheese geddit?)|archivedate=20220221092805 }}</ref> of ''Star Wars'' fan Colin Bishop (@storydroid) on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]].<ref name="Star Wars Show Ep2">{{StarWarsShow|si820rZgxks|Chvrches, Games at Celebration, Star Wars in Japan|sw_url=video/the-star-wars-show-episode-2}}</ref>

===Cameos===
{{Quote|Bro, you know they blew you up after, like, three seconds after you rolled onscreen? You're canonically dead in that outfit.''"<br />"''Yeah, Mr. Big Shot Hollywood guy, hitting shins, thinks he's the king of ''Star Wars'' now, huh?|Andi Gutierrez and Anthony Carboni to CH-33Z in the January 2020 episode of ''The Star Wars Show''|<ref name="SW Show Gaten">{{StarWarsShow|Bau3QI-8dTI|The Star Wars Show Changes Things Up, Plus We Talk With Gaten Matarazzo from Stranger Things|sw_url=video/the-star-wars-show-changes-things-up-plus-we-talk-with-gaten-matarazzo-from-stranger-things}}</ref>}}
[[File:CH-33Z_destroyed_by_Burg.jpg|thumb|right|250px|CH-33Z is destroyed by Burg.]]
CH-33Z was introduced into ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] when he made a brief (and fatal) cameo appearance in "[[Chapter 6: The Prisoner]]," the sixth episode of ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' [[The Mandalorian Season One|Season One]], directed by [[Rick Famuyiwa]] and co-written by Famuyiwa and [[Christopher Yost]] and released on [[Disney+]] on [[December 13]], [[2019]].<ref name="Chapter 6" /> While unidentified in the episode itself, he was identified as CH-33Z in the January 2020 episode of ''The Star Wars Show'', released on the Star Wars YouTube channel on [[January 29]], [[2020]].<ref name="The Star Wars Show" /> The droid made another cameo<ref name="Easter Eggs" /> in "[[Episode 4 (Star Wars: Jedi Temple Challenge)|Episode 4]]" of ''[[Star Wars: Jedi Temple Challenge]]'', released on the [[StarWarsKids.com|Star Wars Kids]] YouTube channel on [[June 24]], 2020.<ref name="JTC-E4" />

